<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Mailer's whole cross-section surface: one method, driven by one Hangfire job.

    MailerAudienceSyncJob stays in Humans.Infrastructure/Jobs because
    UseHumansRecurringJobs names it by concrete type and there is no ISection-style
    discovery seam for jobs yet (design §15 step 6b). A consumer in Base is what forces
    a leaf *project* rather than a Contracts/ folder — a folder would make
    Humans.Infrastructure reference the section and cycle
    (memory/architecture/section-project-cycle-fix.md).

    Nothing else leaves. The dashboard's stats, the import plan/apply pair, the whole
    IMailerLiteService read+write surface and the ten audience classes have no consumer
    outside the section and stay internal behind the assembly boundary.

    References Humans.Interfaces alone: the contract returns an int and takes a
    CancellationToken, so no DTO and no Base vocabulary crosses.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Interfaces\Humans.Interfaces.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
